            "heading": "KIOSKS OF CATANIA",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_nNCnfn": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Long before sparkling water came in a can with a fruit drawn on it, it came from a kiosk on the Catania waterfront. A simple stand, a bottle of carbonated water, a wedge of lemon, a pinch of sea salt stirred in by hand. It's called<em>seltz limone e sale</em>, and in Sicily it's less a beverage category than a memory. The drink you had after the beach. The one your grandfather ordered without needing to ask. The taste that means summer's officially here.<br/><br/></p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
